@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `usca-remedies-and-actions`

-- Tests of usca-remedies-and-actions.l4 (Code Civ. Proc. §§ 20-33).  Each expected value is decided from the section cited above the assertion,
-- before the run.  A failing assertion is a finding.

GIVEN court IS A BOOLEAN
      officer IS A BOOLEAN
      ordinary IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `Purpose of a proceeding`
GIVETH A Remedy
`a remedy` court officer ordinary purpose MEANS
    Remedy WITH
        `administered by a court of justice` IS court
        `administered by a judicial officer empowered for that purpose by the Constitution and statutes of this State` IS officer
        `an ordinary proceeding in a court of justice in which one party prosecutes another` IS ordinary
        purpose IS purpose

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 20: judicial remedies are administered by courts of justice or by judicial officers empowered by the Constitution and statutes`

-- Either limb is enough; neither is not a judicial remedy.
#ASSERT `a remedy is a judicial remedy` (`a remedy` TRUE FALSE FALSE `some other purpose`)
#ASSERT `a remedy is a judicial remedy` (`a remedy` FALSE TRUE FALSE `some other purpose`)
#ASSERT `a remedy is a judicial remedy` (`a remedy` TRUE TRUE FALSE `some other purpose`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a remedy is a judicial remedy` (`a remedy` FALSE FALSE FALSE `some other purpose`))

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 21, § 22, § 23: an action, and every other judicial remedy is a special proceeding`

-- § 22: an ordinary proceeding in a court of justice by which one party prosecutes another for one of the three purposes.
#ASSERT `the class of the judicial remedy` (`a remedy` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the declaration, enforcement or protection of a right`) EQUALS action
#ASSERT `the class of the judicial remedy` (`a remedy` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the redress or prevention of a wrong`) EQUALS action
#ASSERT `the class of the judicial remedy` (`a remedy` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the punishment of a public offense`) EQUALS action
-- § 23: every other remedy is a special proceeding: an ordinary proceeding for some other purpose, or a judicial remedy that is not an ordinary proceeding.
#ASSERT `the class of the judicial remedy` (`a remedy` TRUE FALSE TRUE `some other purpose`) EQUALS `special proceeding`
#ASSERT `the class of the judicial remedy` (`a remedy` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the redress or prevention of a wrong`) EQUALS `special proceeding`
#ASSERT `the class of the judicial remedy` (`a remedy` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the declaration, enforcement or protection of a right`) EQUALS `special proceeding`
-- Outside the encoding: a remedy that is not a judicial remedy (fork F-23).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the class of the judicial remedy` (`a remedy` FALSE FALSE FALSE `some other purpose`) BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 21 divides judicial remedies into actions and special proceedings; a remedy that is not a judicial remedy under § 20 is in neither class on the deposited text"

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 24, § 25, § 30: actions are civil or criminal; a civil action arises out of an obligation or an injury`

#ASSERT `the kind of an action brought for` `the declaration, enforcement or protection of a right` EQUALS civil
#ASSERT `the kind of an action brought for` `the redress or prevention of a wrong` EQUALS civil
#ASSERT `the kind of an action brought for` `the punishment of a public offense` EQUALS criminal
#ASSERT REFUSED `the kind of an action brought for` `some other purpose`
#ASSERT `a civil action may arise out of` obligation
#ASSERT `a civil action may arise out of` injury
#ASSERT REFUSED `a civil action may arise out of` `something else`

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 26: an obligation is a legal duty that binds one person to do or not to do a certain thing and arises from contract or operation of law`

#ASSERT `a duty is an obligation` TRUE TRUE contract
#ASSERT `a duty is an obligation` TRUE TRUE `operation of law`
#ASSERT NOT (`a duty is an obligation` TRUE TRUE `something else`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a duty is an obligation` TRUE FALSE contract)
#ASSERT NOT (`a duty is an obligation` FALSE TRUE contract)
#ASSERT `an obligation may arise from` contract
#ASSERT `an obligation may arise from` `operation of law`
#ASSERT NOT (`an obligation may arise from` `something else`)

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 27, § 28, § 29: an injury is to the person or to property`

-- § 28: the four ways the text names.
#ASSERT `depriving an owner of the benefit of property in the way is a way the text names` taking
#ASSERT `depriving an owner of the benefit of property in the way is a way the text names` withholding
#ASSERT `depriving an owner of the benefit of property in the way is a way the text names` deteriorating
#ASSERT `depriving an owner of the benefit of property in the way is a way the text names` destroying
#ASSERT NOT (`depriving an owner of the benefit of property in the way is a way the text names` `some other way`)
#ASSERT `the kind of an injury` TRUE taking EQUALS `an injury to property`
#ASSERT `the kind of an injury` TRUE withholding EQUALS `an injury to property`
#ASSERT `the kind of an injury` TRUE deteriorating EQUALS `an injury to property`
#ASSERT `the kind of an injury` TRUE destroying EQUALS `an injury to property`
-- § 29: every other injury is an injury to the person.
#ASSERT `the kind of an injury` FALSE taking EQUALS `an injury to the person`
#ASSERT `the kind of an injury` FALSE `some other way` EQUALS `an injury to the person`
-- Outside the encoding: depriving the owner by a way § 28 does not name (fork F-28).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the kind of an injury` TRUE `some other way`

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 31, § 32, § 32.5, § 33`

#ASSERT `the code that defines and provides for the prosecution of a criminal action` EQUALS "the Penal Code"
-- § 32: where both a civil and a criminal remedy are admitted, the right to prosecute the one is not merged in the other.
#ASSERT NOT (`the right to prosecute one remedy is merged in the other` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the right to prosecute one remedy is merged in the other` FALSE
-- § 32.5: the two classifications, and no third.
#ASSERT `the classification is a jurisdictional classification` `a limited civil case`
#ASSERT `the classification is a jurisdictional classification` `an unlimited civil case`
#ASSERT NOT (`the classification is a jurisdictional classification` `some other classification`)
-- § 33: a prosecuting attorney may assist in the civil resolution of a Title 13 offense; for another offense the text does not say.
#ASSERT `a prosecuting attorney may assist in the civil resolution of a violation in lieu of filing a criminal complaint` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `a prosecuting attorney may assist in the civil resolution of a violation in lieu of filing a criminal complaint` FALSE

-- assertions written: 46
